  "claim_short": "Let G be the first Grushin plane and Y={(0,y)} its singular axis. If phi:S^1 -> G is Lipschitz and no nondegenerate segment of Y is contained in a bounded component of R^2 \\ phi(S^1), then phi has a Lipschitz extension to the disk. This gives a full affirmative answer to Question 8.7.",
